  "parts": [
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic streaming speech-to-text task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file stream_microphone.py using AWS.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] stream_microphone.py - streams microphone audio and yields interim transcripts\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] stream_chunks.py - streams audio chunks from an async source\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] partial_results.py - handles partial and final streaming recognition events\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] stream_with_language.py - starts a streaming recognizer with language and punctuation settings\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] speech_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Streaming Speech-to-Text\n6. [HELPER] speech_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Streaming Speech-to-Text\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] live_caption_translate.py - Translate live captions into another language\n8. [LATER-STEP] live_caption_safety.py - Check live transcript text for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] meeting_summary.py - Summarize live meeting transcript chunks\n10. [LATER-STEP] caption_embedding.py - Embed caption chunks for semantic meeting search\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
